---
### Context-Free Grammars
Four components, written using **Backus–Naur Form (BNF)**:
...
{size=27px} - **{{color=neon_blue|Terminal symbols}}:** tokens. The symbol ε denotes the empty string.
...
{size=27px} - **{{color=neon_blue|Nonterminal symbols}}:** syntactic variables.
...
{size=27px} - **{{color=neon_blue|Start symbol S}}:** a distinguished nonterminal.
...
{size=27px} - **{{color=neon_blue|Production rules}}:** LHS → RHS.
...
  {size=25px} - LHS: a single nonterminal.
  {size=25px} - RHS: a string of terminals and nonterminals.
  {size=25px} - A production specifies how to expand a nonterminal.
@(880, 300) {w=310px, size=25px, pad=12px, fill=#102233, color=#F4F1E8, stroke=#31505F} ```
S → a S a
S → T
T → b S b
T → ε
```
...
[language] @(84, 582) {size=25px, w=1090px} The language generated by a grammar is the set of terminal strings derived from the start symbol by repeatedly applying productions.
[lg] @(84, 669) {size=24px, w=1090px, color=id} $L(G)$ = the language generated by grammar $G$
---
% PowerPoint slides 9.
### Context-Free Grammar Example
Grammar for balanced parentheses:
{w=1112px, size=29px, pad=12px, fill=#102233, color=#F4F1E8, stroke=#31505F} ```
S → ( S ) S
S → ε
```
...
{size=27px} One nonterminal: **{{color=neon_pink|S}}**. Two terminals: **{{color=neon_green|(}}** and **{{color=neon_green|)}}**. Start symbol: **{{color=neon_pink|S}}**. Two productions.
...
{size=27px} An accepted string has a derivation using these production rules.
...
How do we produce **{{color=neon_green|(())}}**?
...
[derive] @(84, 540) {size=34px, w=1110px, color=id} {{color=neon_pink|S}}
...
!anim derive text {{color=neon_green|(}} {{color=neon_pink|S}} {{color=neon_green|)}} {{color=neon_pink|S}}
...
!anim derive text {{color=neon_green|(}} {{color=neon_pink|S}} {{color=neon_green|)}} {{color=neon_blue|ε}}
...
!anim derive text {{color=neon_green|( (}} {{color=neon_pink|S}} {{color=neon_green|)}} {{color=neon_pink|S}} {{color=neon_green|)}} {{color=neon_blue|ε}}
...
!anim derive text {{color=neon_green|( (}} ε {{color=neon_green|)}} {{color=neon_blue|ε}} {{color=neon_green|)}} {{color=neon_blue|ε}}
...
!anim derive text {{color=neon_green|(())}}
---
### More on Context-Free Grammars
...
Use a vertical bar `|` as shorthand for alternative productions:
{w=1112px, size=30px, pad=12px, fill=#102233, color=#F4F1E8, stroke=#31505F} ```
S → a S a | T
T → b T b | ε
```
...
- {{color=emp|CFGs}} can express the syntax of most programming languages.
...
- **{{color=emp|Derivation}}:** successive application of productions, starting from S.
...
- **{{color=emp|Acceptance}}:** determine whether an input token stream has a derivation.

