% PowerPoint slides 12.
### Regular Expressions Are a Subset of CFGs
{size=27px} We can inductively build a context-free grammar for every regular expression.
...
{w=1112px, size=27px, pad=10px, headerfill=#173749, headertext=#F4F1E8, bodytext=#F4F1E8, stripe=#102233} | Regular expression | Equivilent production |  |
|:---|:---|:---|
| ε | S → ε | |
| a | S → a | |
| R₁ R₂ | S → S₁ S₂ | |
| R₁ &#124; R₂ | S → S₁ &#124; S₂ | |
| R₁* | S → S₁′ | S₁′ → S₁ S₁′ &#124; ε |
...
{size=26px} G₁ is the grammar for R₁, with start symbol S₁.{{br}}G₂ is the grammar for R₂, with start symbol S₂.

